The first two rows are references, not candidates: what a conventional
vector stack scores, and what Engram ships. Every `bench:` row below them
reads the same store and the same embeddings, so a difference is a
difference in ranking strategy and nothing else. Indented rows change one
thing from the row above the group. `obliq` — recall on questions that
never name their subject — is the column the shipped stack loses on and
therefore the only one worth beating rag in.

